Code Red: the PokÉEG in the game (owner, 2026-10-09). A PC screen listing every Pokémon
the player owns (party, then the boxes) and, for the one under the cursor, a look inside
its mind: its type's system, readers learned, Pokédex readers, byte budget, focus, the
last ten turns (hit/miss) and its hot memory. The game asks the page through a mailbox
(struct CodeRedEeg, 164 B) one Pokémon at a time; hot memory is typed on the page.
Menu entries live in patch 003 (PC menu, bedroom PC); this patch is the screen itself.
No host → the mind lines say so; the list still works.
diff --git a/src/code_red_eeg.c b/src/code_red_eeg.c
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..590c76ca
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/code_red_eeg.c
@@ -0,0 +1,630 @@
+// Code Red: the PokÉEG, in the game (owner, 2026-10-09). From the PC: every Pokémon the player
+// owns (party, then the boxes), and for the one under the cursor a look inside its mind.
+// The game knows the Pokémon; the page knows the mind (readers, hot memory, code history live in the
+// cloud save). So this screen asks the page through a mailbox, one Pokémon at a time, and draws what
+// comes back. Hot memory is typed on the page (a note can be 200 characters; the naming screen can't).
+// No host → the mind lines stay blank; the screen still works as a list.
+#include "global.h"
+#include "gflib.h"
+#include "data.h"
+#include "decompress.h"
+#include "graphics.h"
+#include "help_system.h"
